      en: "Tongyeong is a port city in Gyeongsangnam Province on the south coast, known for the Tongyeong Naval Battle Memorial Park, commemorating Admiral Yi Sun-sin's victories during the Imjin Wars. The city lies on Hansando Island and is surrounded by numerous islands and bays. Economically, fishing (especially oyster and fish farming), shipbuilding, and tourism are important. Population is about 130,000. Tongyeong is also known for its traditional lacquerware art (Najeonchilgi) and the annual Tongyeong International Music Festival. Geographically, it belongs to Hallyeohaesang National Park.",
