      en: "Miryang is a city in Gyeongsangnam Province, known for the Miryang Ice Valley (Eoreumgol), a natural cold phenomenon where ice persists until summer. The city also hosts Miryang Palace and Mea-ri Shrine. Geographically, it lies in the Miryanggang River valley, surrounded by Cheonhwangsan and Jaeyaksan Mountains. Economically, agriculture (rice, persimmons, watermelons) and tourism are significant. Population is about 100,000. Miryang is also known for the annual Miryang Arirang Festival and traditional Korean music. The city has a rich literary history as the birthplace of poet Kim Satgat.",
